{
  "title": "Split CookbookPage by responsibility",
  "description": "ramekin-ui/src/pages/CookbookPage.tsx is roughly 1,400 lines \
and currently owns query parsing and serialization, filter input state, \
request and pagination state, infinite scrolling, random navigation, bulk \
selection and fetching, PDF export coordination, and the full page render \
tree. The concentration makes async correctness changes difficult to review \
and test; the stale-response bug is one example.\n\
\n\
Scope:\n\
- Extract cohesive units around query/filter serialization, recipe-list \
request state, bulk-selection operations, filter controls, and recipe-grid \
rendering. Follow existing SolidJS patterns and keep state ownership \
explicit.\n\
- Preserve current URL behavior, responsive behavior, accessibility, and API \
request shapes.\n\
- Move existing pure helpers into focused modules with unit tests before \
moving reactive orchestration.\n\
- Keep this mechanical: no visual redesign, new controls, state-management \
dependency, or API changes.\n\
- Run web unit and UI tests, including mobile and desktop cookbook coverage.\n\
\n\
This is web-only structural cleanup; there is no equivalent iOS change to \
mirror.",
